  "name": "Godot Engine",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "Development",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "Godot_v4.exe",
      "godot.windows.editor.x86_64.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "org.godotengine.godot"
    ],
    "window_title": []
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/editor/default_key_mapping.html",
    "https://docs.godotengine.org/en/4.5/tutorials/editor/default_key_mapping.html"
  ],
  "note": "From the official Godot Engine 4.5 docs (\"stable\" branch resolves to 4.5 as of this writing) 'Default editor shortcuts' page, which the docs mark as work-in-progress and possibly not fully updated for 4.5. Omitted as not expressible by the chord grammar: numpad-bound view/grid shortcuts (Multiply/Divide grid step by 2 = Num* / Num/; Top/Bottom/Front/Rear/Right/Left View and Switch Perspective/Orthogonal View = Num 7/1/3/5 with Alt variants), bare held-modifier shortcuts (3D Editor Freelook Speed Modifier = Shift alone, Freelook Slow Modifier = Alt/Opt alone), and Pan View (Space held while dragging with the mouse). Two 'Select Mode'/'Move Mode'/'Rotate Mode' pairs and other same-named actions are intentionally duplicated across the 2D Editor and 3D Editor contexts because Godot binds them independently per editor.",
